From 7b0bc7250c6f529d4eee91aa7005767e72a54a70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: callan <callanf@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:59:37 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 04/38] feat(engine): class-aware scheduling (class order in
 the waiting queue, class preemption), off by default

EngineConfig.class_scheduling {order, preempt_max_rank}: requests carry a policy_class; the
vLLM-style waiting queue is kept in (class rank, arrival) order and a preempted request rejoins at
the front of its own class. With preempt_max_rank, a waiting request ranked at or above it that
cannot get blocks or a sequence slot preempts running requests ranked below it (lowest class,
newest first) before the pass, and KV-pressure preemption takes the lowest class first. Engine and
replay requests gain an optional policy_class, forwarded from the replay request. Without
class_scheduling the engine is unchanged.
